This task involves standardizing the soft-delete implementation across the application:

1. Consolidate soft-delete approach:
   - Review current implementations across entities (companies, projects, meetings, action-items)
   - Standardize on Boolean `isDeleted` field for all entities
   - Document rationale for Boolean vs Integer approach:
     ```markdown
     ## Soft-Delete Implementation Decision

     ### Boolean Approach (Recommended)
     - **Implementation**: `isDeleted: boolean` (true/false)
     - **Advantages**:
       - Simpler semantics - an item is either deleted or not
       - Clearer API contracts - no ambiguity about deletion state
       - Better type safety in TypeScript
       - More intuitive for frontend filtering
     - **Disadvantages**:
       - Cannot track deletion history or multiple deletion states

     ### Integer Approach
     - **Implementation**: `deletionStatus: number` (0=active, 1=soft-deleted, 2=marked for hard delete, etc.)
     - **Advantages**:
       - Supports multiple deletion states or workflow stages
       - Can represent more complex state transitions
     - **Disadvantages**:
       - Less intuitive API semantics
       - Requires documentation to understand status codes
       - More complex filtering logic
     ```

2. Define backend implementation standards:
   - Update database schemas to use `isDeleted: boolean` with default value `false`
   - Ensure all entity controllers filter by default: `WHERE isDeleted = false`
   - Add optional query parameter to include deleted items: `?includeDeleted=true`
   - Implement soft-delete endpoints that update the flag rather than removing records
   - Document standard SQL queries for retrieving/filtering deleted items

3. Create frontend implementation guidelines:
   - Define standard API query parameters for filtering:
     ```typescript
     // Example API call with deletion filtering
     const getProjects = async (includeDeleted = false) => {
       return api.get('/projects', { params: { includeDeleted } });
     };
     ```
   - Provide Pinia store patterns for handling deleted items:
     ```typescript
     // Store definition example
     export const useProjectStore = defineStore('projects', {
       state: () => ({
         projects: [],
         includeDeleted: false
       }),
       getters: {
         visibleProjects: (state) => state.includeDeleted 
           ? state.projects 
           : state.projects.filter(p => !p.isDeleted)
       },
       actions: {
         async fetchProjects() {
           const { data } = await api.get('/projects', { 
             params: { includeDeleted: this.includeDeleted } 
           });
           this.projects = data;
         },
         async softDeleteProject(id) {
           await api.patch(`/projects/${id}`, { isDeleted: true });
           // Update local state
           const project = this.projects.find(p => p.id === id);
           if (project) project.isDeleted = true;
         },
         async restoreProject(id) {
           await api.patch(`/projects/${id}`, { isDeleted: false });
           // Update local state
           const project = this.projects.find(p => p.id === id);
           if (project) project.isDeleted = false;
         }
       }
     });
     ```

4. Define UI representation standards:
   - Provide component examples for displaying deleted items:
     ```vue
     <template>
       <div>
         <div class="filter-controls">
           <v-checkbox v-model="showDeleted" label="Show deleted items" />
         </div>

         <v-data-table :items="visibleItems">
           <template v-slot:item="{ item }">
             <tr :class="{ 'deleted-item': item.isDeleted }">
               <td>{{ item.name }}</td>
               <td>
                 <v-chip v-if="item.isDeleted" color="red" small>Deleted</v-chip>
               </td>
               <td>
                 <v-btn v-if="item.isDeleted" @click="restoreItem(item.id)">
                   Restore
                 </v-btn>
                 <v-btn v-else @click="deleteItem(item.id)">
                   Delete
                 </v-btn>
               </td>
             </tr>
           </template>
         </v-data-table>
       </div>
     </template>

     <script setup>
     import { ref, computed } from 'vue';
     import { useItemStore } from '@/stores/items';

     const itemStore = useItemStore();
     const showDeleted = ref(false);

     // Update store when checkbox changes
     watch(showDeleted, (newValue) => {
       itemStore.includeDeleted = newValue;
       itemStore.fetchItems();
     });

     const visibleItems = computed(() => {
       return showDeleted.value 
         ? itemStore.items 
         : itemStore.items.filter(item => !item.isDeleted);
     });

     const deleteItem = (id) => itemStore.softDeleteItem(id);
     const restoreItem = (id) => itemStore.restoreItem(id);
     </script>

     <style>
     .deleted-item {
       opacity: 0.6;
       text-decoration: line-through;
     }
     </style>
     ```

